{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And he sent the raven.</b> Because its way is to eat carrion, and if the waters had subsided, it would find corpses of the flood cast upon the face of the water. One should not object: how did he send it, when there is no light in the world? This is not so, for even though the constellations — namely sun, moon, and stars — did not serve, and there was no distinction between day and night, nevertheless there was light. A proof for the matter: the tops of the mountains were seen. And furthermore, there are those who say in Bereshit Rabbah that they did serve, but their mark was not discernible. Even so, the Sages asked: how did Noah know during the flood to distinguish between day and night?" "<b>And it went forth, going and returning.</b> Resh Lakish said: the raven gave Noah an eternal rebuff. It said to him: your Master hates me, and you hate me. Your Master hates me — for He commanded to take of the pure seven pairs and of the impure two pairs; and you hate me — for you left the seven and sent one of us two. Therefore: ויצא יצוא ושוב."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:28.115486091Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}